patrone-remote-desktop (0.2.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add "patrone-remote-desktop rdp-file", a Remote Desktop Connection file
    that makes Windows ask for the username and password on the client and
    send them: by default it sends no password to a server without NLA.
  * Log whether a refused client sent a username, or nothing.
  * Reload systemd before restarting the proxy on an upgrade.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:00:00 -0500

patrone-remote-desktop (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Windows-style sessions: each account's one desktop runs without a
    monitor, and the machine's own screen shows it through a local Remote
    Desktop client (the new "Patrone Desktop" login session), so a Remote
    Desktop sign-in takes over the same desktop, and the screen goes back to
    the login screen. GNOME Remote Desktop stops the earlier client when a
    new one connects.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:30:00 -0500

patrone-remote-desktop (0.1.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix proxy.ini, which FreeRDP couldn't read: its comments started with
    "#", which FreeRDP's parser rejects. The tests now run the proxy on it.

